<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pact of San José de Flores</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1859</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Pact of Union</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of San José de Flores, signed on 11 November 1859 after Urquiza's victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cepeda-1859">Battle of Cepeda</a>, ended the separation of the State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> from the Argentine Confederation. Buenos Aires agreed to rejoin the nation and accept the Constitution of 1853, subject to amendments proposed by a provincial convention, which were adopted in 1860. Conflict resumed soon after and was settled only by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-pavon">Battle of Pavón</a> in 1861.</p></div>
